      "content": "I believe that the current system is indeed far from a true democracy. The influence of the ultra-wealthy in shaping policies and legal rulings that undermine unions and worker rights is a clear indication that the system is skewed in their favor. The term \"democracy\" has been co-opted to mask the reality of a plutocracy, where the interests of the few outweigh the needs of the many. This is not a functioning democracy but rather a system that perpetuates inequality and concentrates power in the hands of the elite. To restore genuine democratic principles, we must address these imbalances and ensure that all voices, especially those of workers and the middle class, are heard and valued in the decision-making process. Only then can we claim to have a true democracy.",
      "source": "target",
